# NextCNC Cursor Rules

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Source Control Rules (READ FIRST)

### 🚫 NEVER COMMIT WITHOUT EXPLICIT PERMISSION
**YOU MUST NEVER commit, push, or modify git history unless explicitly instructed to do so by the user.**

- **❌ DO NOT** run `git commit`, `git push`, or any git commands that modify repository state
- **❌ DO NOT** check in code proactively or "helpfully"
- **❌ DO NOT** commit fixes, updates, or changes without being asked
- **✅ ONLY** commit when the user explicitly says "check in", "commit", or similar

**Consequences of violating this rule:**
- Repository corruption
- Lost work
- Team conflicts
- Breaking CI/CD pipelines

**If you need to commit:** Wait for explicit user instruction. Do not suggest or offer to commit.

---

## Project Context
CNCjs frontend modernization — replacing legacy React/Webpack with modern React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui. Backend is Express + Socket.IO (mostly unchanged).

---

## Model identification

Always report which model and which version you are at the end of each response

---

## 🛑 Protected Code (CRITICAL)

**Do NOT modify these paths without explicit user permission:**
- `apps/server/src/controllers/**` — All CNC controller implementations
- `apps/server/src/lib/Sender.js` — G-code streaming engine
- `apps/server/src/lib/Feeder.js` — Real-time command queue
- `apps/server/src/lib/Workflow.js` — Workflow state machine
- `apps/server/src/lib/SerialConnection.js` — Serial port communication
- `apps/server/src/lib/EventTrigger.js` — Event trigger system
- `apps/server/src/lib/MessageSlot.js` — M0/M1 pause handling

These are safety-critical G-code sender components. Bugs can cause machine crashes, tool breakage, or injury. See `ai/docs/protected-code.md` for details.

**If you need to modify protected code:** Stop, explain what you want to change and why, then wait for explicit permission.

---

## Build & Development

**Never start or stop dev servers** — Always ask the user to start/stop servers. Do not run `cd apps/web && yarn dev`, `yarn dev:start-server`, or kill/restart any running processes. Just tell the user what to run and they will handle it.

---

## Code Conventions

### Frontend (apps/web/)
- Use existing shadcn/ui components before creating new ones
- Follow patterns in existing code — check similar files first
- TypeScript for all new code
- RTK Query for API calls (`apps/web/src/services/api.ts`)

### Naming
- Handlers: `handle{Action}` (e.g., `handleLanguageChange`)
- Props callbacks: `on{Action}` (e.g., `onLanguageChange`)
- Boolean state: `is{State}` or descriptive (e.g., `isSaving`, `allowAnalytics`)

---

## File Structure

```
apps/
├── web/                    # Modern frontend (work here)
│   └── src/
│       ├── components/     # Reusable UI components
│       ├── routes/         # Page components
│       ├── services/       # API and Socket.IO
│       └── store/          # Redux store
├── server/                 # Backend (protected, mostly unchanged)
│   └── src/
│       ├── controllers/    # CNC controllers (PROTECTED)
│       ├── lib/            # Core libs (PROTECTED)
│       └── api/            # REST API endpoints
├── desktop/                # Electron app
│   └── src/
packages/
└── shared/                 # Shared schemas and utilities
    └── src/
ai/
├── docs/                   # Project documentation
├── personas/               # AI agent personas
└── plans/                  # Project plans
website/
├── static/                 # Static website files (deployed to GitHub Pages)
└── docs/                   # User documentation (will generate to static/docs)
```

